{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/43810-looking-for-your-opinion-on-an-old-work","id":43810,"title":"Looking for your opinion on an old work","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-06T17:24:47-08:00","id":43810,"title":"Looking for your opinion on an old work","content":"A few years and a couple of forum's iterations ago, under the name of Atomic Hermit, I started to write a fan made pantheon based on H.P. Lovecraft's creations. I was helped by many other forumites, mostly Man in Black (<i>especially</i> him), Baron Samedi and Dean Shomshak. Life got in the way and I never really finished it, but I've just found that old file in a lonely CD and thought that, since it was almost completed, huge even in its incomplete shape and, most importantly, that most of those who read it liked it a lot, I might clear it up a little, share it and see how things go.<br /> <br /> Back in the days, most of the criticism came from the fact that fictional pantheons don't really work in Scion but, from the first day, I wrote under the assumption that it would only be used by those who were looking for something different to add to their game. I've tried to put Cthulhu into Scion by working around the canon in order to minimize the massive impact his presence would have in the game and I think I did a decent job, but it's not going to work if you're not willing to play along. I've never tried to say otherwise.<br /> <br /> On the other side, the supplement takes quite a few liberties (heresies, some would say <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) with Lovecraft's works. Things like Cthulhu and Azathoth belonging to the same magnitude of beings while there's a distinction between Great Old Ones and Outer Gods, giving them a semblance of a &quot;not-completely-alien&quot; personality, describing some facts in spite of Lovecraft's love for the unknown and contradictions, ignoring some elements of the Cthulhu Mythos as a whole...that sort of things. Not to mention the stuff I've made up myself. Why I did it? Here's why: to made them playable and <i>fun </i>to play while trying to give people what they were looking for and, at the same time, trying to remain faithful to both the original source and the Scion's setting.<br /> <br /> Basically, it's something that tries to find a middle ground between two deeply different settings, a shift from both of them made in the name of light-hearted fun. A &quot;Shard&quot;, if I can steal the term from WoD and Exalted.<br /> <br /> If, after all this, you're still interested, just let me know and I'll post it. So, what do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-06-2014, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T05:12:48-08:00","id":44085,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see that - it'd be a nice distraction from endless conversations on the Abramahic pantheon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, it opens the door to a lot of interesting interactions with &quot;traditional&quot; pantheons, either as antagonists or strange contacts.<br /> I think it might be particularly appropriate in the context of Origins as well - I'm thinking of such stories as The Mountains of Madness, where finding the traces of an old, alien city in Antarctica could be the visitation of an exploring scion of Hermes and his first contact with monstruous titanspawn...<br /> <br /> Plus, lovecraft's mythos is so alien that it sort of merges well with most stuff - there was even a Queen K'tula in Exalted after all, which makes a rather interesting (and challenging!) antagonist, a bit different from the usual Deathlords...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1609-fumble","name":"Fumble","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T10:01:04-08:00","id":44258,"title":"","content":"Hi there, long time no see!<br /> <br /> Sure bring it up, maybe it will activate the creative juices within me and others. Participating in the creation process, seeing feedback and the exchange of ideas is one of my joys in life (take the hint and go comment on the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/34636-the-occuria-ficticious-pantheon#post34636\">Occuria</a>).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumble</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/43810-looking-for-your-opinion-on-an-old-work?p=44085#post44085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see that - it'd be a nice distraction from endless conversations on the Abramahic pantheon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T10:32:03-08:00","id":44273,"title":"","content":"I don't much like Lovecraft, but this sounds very interesting. I'm especially curious as to how you divided the Titan from Gods, which always strikes me as the biggest hurdle for adapting Mythos to Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:31:53-08:00","id":44364,"title":"","content":"Welcome back! Sure, polish it up and re-post the material. <br /> <br /> I don't think HPL would mind your re-imagining of his Mythos: He was pretty playful about it himself. <br /> <br /> I don't mind &quot;Shard&quot; approaches to Scion either, so long as the creators acknowledge that they are playing around with alternate visions. It's when people insist that core Scion *must* include a Superhero Pantheon or whatever that I get tetchy. I think your Cthulhu Shard is a lot of fun! <br /> <br /> (And I'm glad I could help before. You're welcome.) Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T17:54:41-08:00","id":47159,"title":"","content":"Very well then. As soon as I'm done with my Latin exam, I'll get to work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumble</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/43810-looking-for-your-opinion-on-an-old-work?p=44085#post44085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it opens the door to a lot of interesting interactions with &quot;traditional&quot; pantheons, either as antagonists or strange contacts.<br /> I think it might be particularly appropriate in the context of Origins as well - I'm thinking of such stories as The Mountains of Madness, where finding the traces of an old, alien city in Antarctica could be the visitation of an exploring scion of Hermes and his first contact with monstruous titanspawn...<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. When I've used this pantheon in my campaign, its biggest contribution to the game was perhaps the host of &quot;unconventional&quot; possibilities it gave to me and my players. They were Scions of other pantheons, but this only increased the alien mood surrounding the Great Old Ones whenever they came up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Man in Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/43810-looking-for-your-opinion-on-an-old-work?p=44258#post44258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hi there, long time no see!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello! Yeah, it's been quite a while, I'm more a lurker than an active member of the community, not to mention that after the end of our Scion campaign, my group moved to other gamelines and I lost sight of the Scion forum. This new site seemed a good excuse to return.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Man in Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/43810-looking-for-your-opinion-on-an-old-work?p=44258#post44258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Participating in the creation process, seeing feedback and the exchange of ideas is one of my joys in life (take the hint and go comment on the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/34636-the-occuria-ficticious-pantheon#post34636\">Occuria</a>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/43810-looking-for-your-opinion-on-an-old-work?p=44273#post44273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't much like Lovecraft, but this sounds very interesting. I'm especially curious as to how you divided the Titan from Gods, which always strikes me as the biggest hurdle for adapting Mythos to Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can prove to be quite a hurdle, yes. In my case, the quick answer is that they were Fatebound from Titan material into Godhood by the works of Lovecraft and its literary circle, which somehow tied such inhuman beings to mankind. The pantheon's history is more complex than that, but that's to give you an idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/43810-looking-for-your-opinion-on-an-old-work?p=44364#post44364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welcome back! Sure, polish it up and re-post the material.<br /> <br /> I don't think HPL would mind your re-imagining of his Mythos: He was pretty playful about it himself.<br /> <br /> I don't mind &quot;Shard&quot; approaches to Scion either, so long as the creators acknowledge that they are playing around with alternate visions. It's when people insist that core Scion *must* include a Superhero Pantheon or whatever that I get tetchy. I think your Cthulhu Shard is a lot of fun!<br /> <br /> (And I'm glad I could help before. You're welcome.) Dean Shomshak</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks, Dean. I really need to polish it up, since my English improved a bit after all these years and some of the ideas I had back then seem quite odd now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-11-2014, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}